<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:11:04 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Focus</category><title>With new law, Iraq sees rise in child marriage, custody battles</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261127-with-new-law-iraq-sees-rise-in-child-marriage-custody-battles</link><description>
In January 2025, Iraq's parliament passed an amendment allowing families to place their household under religious law, governing all issues around marriage, divorce and inheritance. The new Ja'fari law, a Shiite law, came into force in October 2025. One year on, its consequences have been raising serious alarm, especially among women, who say they've seen a major rollback of their rights. FRANCE 24's Marie-Charlotte Roupie reports, with Josh Vardey.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/377a84f8-ea66-11f1-af1d-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-077060cd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/377a84f8-ea66-11f1-af1d-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-077060cd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6eb4a8e2-e9bf-11f1-afdb-d70a1ec89236</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:48:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marie-Charlotte ROUPIE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel's Eisenkot agrees to coalition deal with left-wing Democrats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261127-israel-s-eisenkot-agrees-to-coalition-deal-with-left-wing-democrats</link><description>
Israel's former military chief Gadi Eisenkot on Thursday struck a coalition deal with Yair Golan's left-leaning Democrats, bringing the country's opposition closer to forming a government after no single bloc secured a majority in the October elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/173042bc-ea1d-11f1-92b3-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T134206Z-1084090684-RC2OTOAAPLPQ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS-NETANYAHU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/173042bc-ea1d-11f1-92b3-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T134206Z-1084090684-RC2OTOAAPLPQ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS-NETANYAHU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dbe58d44-ea2a-11f1-8bd7-c9c69014f67e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:46:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/173042bc-ea1d-11f1-92b3-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T134206Z-1084090684-RC2OTOAAPLPQ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS-NETANYAHU.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hamas weighs response after Israel kills 10 people in Gaza</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/hamas-weighs-response-after-israel-kills-10-people-in-gaza</link><description>
Five Israeli strikes and a shooting overnight and on Thursday killed 10 Palestinians across Gaza, according to officials at Shifa and Al-Aqsa Martyrs hospitals, where the casualties were taken. A strike on a residential apartment in Deir Al-Balah in central Gaza killed a man and his wife, the officials said. FRANCE 24's Jennie Shin speaks with journalist Ahmed Dremly, who was in Gaza until six months ago and has extensively covered the humanitarian crisis there.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4351c01e-e9d7-11f1-a478-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-210731-211826-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4351c01e-e9d7-11f1-a478-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-210731-211826-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48ad2918-e9d7-11f1-ab34-f19fc60df09a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:35:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel threatens to displace one million Palestinians in Gaza unless Hamas disarms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261126-israel-threatens-to-displace-one-million-palestinians-in-gaza-unless-hamas-disarms</link><description>
Israel's defence minister on Thursday threatened to forcibly displace one million Palestinians in Gaza if Hamas does not move to voluntarily surrender its weapons, as previously promised. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd677e20-e991-11f1-9957-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T181446Z-1897406615-RC2PTOAHCOHO-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd677e20-e991-11f1-9957-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T181446Z-1897406615-RC2PTOAHCOHO-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d885ac5c-e993-11f1-b8f0-697d64a0b135</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:28:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd677e20-e991-11f1-9957-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T181446Z-1897406615-RC2PTOAHCOHO-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg">© Mahmoud Issa, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iraqi court sentences 8 French nationals to life in prison for IS group membership</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261126-iraqi-court-to-sentence-20-french-nationals-for-is-group-membership</link><description>
An Iraqi court sentenced eight French nationals to life in prison and two others to 15 years on Thursday for joining the Islamic State group, as Baghdad steps up prosecutions of thousands of alleged jihadists transferred from Syria.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e60ee952-e960-11f1-829c-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19153526752150.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e60ee952-e960-11f1-829c-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19153526752150.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a96c6cc4-e95e-11f1-8b02-1bf770abc0af</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:28:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e60ee952-e960-11f1-829c-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19153526752150.jpg">© Khalid Mohammed, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli lawmakers advance October 7 inquiry opposed by Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-lawmakers-advance-october-7-inquiry-opposed-by-netanyahu</link><description>
Israel's new parliament on Wednesday took a first step to set up a state commission of inquiry into the security failures that led to Hamas's unprecedented October 7, 2023 attack, a move long opposed by caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30dabc2c-d09d-11f1-a1eb-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T174015Z-1419027181-RC2T9OAZQPTJ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-RALLY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30dabc2c-d09d-11f1-a1eb-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T174015Z-1419027181-RC2T9OAZQPTJ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-RALLY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">deb33278-e91d-11f1-bbce-f955831d9273</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:26:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In boost for Netanyahu, judges question corruption trial charges</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/in-boost-for-netanyahu-judges-question-corruption-trial-charges</link><description>
Judges in the long-running corruption trial of Israeli caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu handed his defence a major boost on Wednesday in recommending the prosecution drop one of the cases in which he is accused of bribery. The recommendations, which came as Israel's longest-serving prime minister fights for his political survival, were immediately cheered by Netanyahu's right-wing allies who demanded the trial be brought to an end. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc479688-e905-11f1-9b30-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-201038-201315-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc479688-e905-11f1-9b30-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-201038-201315-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1ce860c-e905-11f1-b91f-3305ae4b2a65</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:28:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Libya’s Haftar visits old foe Turkey for first time in ‘new phase’ of ties</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261125-libya-s-haftar-visits-old-foe-turkey-in-a-first-hails-new-phase-of-ties</link><description>
Eastern Libya military commander Khalifa Haftar met Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan in Ankara on Wednesday during his first official visit to Turkey, marking a major thaw in relations between the longtime rivals. The visit came days after Ukraine struck a Russian warship in Benghazi, a port city controlled by Haftar.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a319b25e-e900-11f1-8c6b-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/f72d2eb3b332f9447b99127eb2578ee67c9a340c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a319b25e-e900-11f1-8c6b-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/f72d2eb3b332f9447b99127eb2578ee67c9a340c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">967a6786-e8e3-11f1-8253-cb2d864e59f7</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:19:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a319b25e-e900-11f1-8c6b-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/f72d2eb3b332f9447b99127eb2578ee67c9a340c.jpg">© AFP via Turkish Presidental Press Service </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli MPs advance bill for inquiry into security failings that led to October 7 Hamas attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261125-israeli-mps-advance-bill-for-inquiry-into-security-failings-that-led-to-october-7-hamas-attack</link><description>
Israeli MPs on Wednesday gave their initial approval for the creation of a commission to investigate the security failures that led to the October 7, 2023 attack by Hamas. Caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who was in power when the attack happened, has repeatedly rejected calls to set up such a probe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b73ba14-e8cf-11f1-aebf-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D8KK3YA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b73ba14-e8cf-11f1-aebf-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D8KK3YA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d06cb4a-e8cf-11f1-9f49-1f7ee7bc6d05</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:55:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2b73ba14-e8cf-11f1-aebf-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D8KK3YA.jpg">© Ilia Yefimovich, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Amnesty calls for ICC genocide probe over Israel's impact on births in Gaza</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261125-amnesty-calls-for-icc-genocide-probe-over-israel-s-impact-on-births-in-gaza</link><description>
Amnesty International on Wednesday urged the International Criminal Court to investigate whether Israeli officials committed genocide in Gaza, citing measures it says have prevented births and severely harmed women's reproductive health. The rights group said it had serious concerns that these effects were intentional, while acknowledging it could not reach a definitive conclusion.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/456077bc-a605-11f1-b43e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6ZG6V4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/456077bc-a605-11f1-b43e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6ZG6V4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f060e892-e884-11f1-afe2-1f07c5efc05b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:01:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/456077bc-a605-11f1-b43e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6ZG6V4.jpg">© Eyad Baba, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen’s army says Houthi fighters closing in on government stronghold of Aden</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261124-yemen-army-houthi-attack-aden</link><description>
Yemen's military on Tuesday said that Houthi fighters were closing in on the internationally recognised government's stronghold of Aden from about 60km (40 miles) away and vowed to repel any assault. A military spokesman said defences were prepared following Houthi advances and government pullbacks near the Red Sea.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4547a760-e961-11f1-9de7-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T142116Z-1374332128-RC22VOAEZ5QY-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-HOUTHI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4547a760-e961-11f1-9de7-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T142116Z-1374332128-RC22VOAEZ5QY-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-HOUTHI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e2418d3e-e820-11f1-950f-8f34280c71c0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:51:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4547a760-e961-11f1-9de7-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T142116Z-1374332128-RC22VOAEZ5QY-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-HOUTHI.jpg">© Planet Labs PBC via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>'We are ready to facilitate removal of Netanyahu': Head of Israel's Arab-majority Joint List</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261124-we-are-ready-to-facilitate-the-removal-of-netanyahu-from-power-head-of-israel-s-joint-list</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, the head of the Arab-majority Joint List said his political alliance is prepared to play a decisive role in bringing down Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's government following the recent election. "We are ready to facilitate the removal of Netanyahu" from power, Yousef Jabareen said, signalling a willingness to explore political alliances beyond traditional divisions in Israeli politics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25fa58f2-e818-11f1-b949-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/photojabareen.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25fa58f2-e818-11f1-b949-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/photojabareen.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a042780-e815-11f1-84b2-47349288adbb</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:29:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli strikes on Gaza kill senior Hamas security official and six other people, medics say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261124-israeli-strikes-on-gaza-kill-senior-hamas-security-official-and-six-other-people-medics-say</link><description>
Israeli air strikes on the devastated Gaza Strip killed Brigadier General Naeem Abu Nahel, director-general of the Palestinian territory's Internal Security Service on Tuesday, the ministry said. Another six people, including two police officers and a 17-year-old teenager, were killed in Israeli strikes across the enclave. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/627512ce-e802-11f1-ad6d-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7J44LE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/627512ce-e802-11f1-ad6d-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7J44LE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e0aa944-e7ff-11f1-b48e-2dd334c20496</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:07:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/627512ce-e802-11f1-ad6d-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7J44LE.jpg">© Bashar Taleb, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel’s Eisenkot slams ‘Jewish terrorism’ after attacks by settlers in West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-israel-s-eisenkot-slams-jewish-terrorism-after-attacks-by-settlers-in-west-bank</link><description>
Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot on Sunday condemned arson attacks by settlers on Palestinian villages in the West Bank as “Jewish terrorism”. Israeli police said they opened an investigation into the attacks, which came nearly a month after an inconclusive election stripped incumbent Prime Minister ⁠Benjamin Netanyahu of his majority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eff41172-e6b8-11f1-a8e7-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326377291946.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eff41172-e6b8-11f1-a8e7-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326377291946.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29c45bc8-e6b9-11f1-8d4a-479735d131b5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:29:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eff41172-e6b8-11f1-a8e7-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26326377291946.jpg">© Mahmoud Illean, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>West Bank attacks: Opposition leader Eisenkot decries "Jewish terrorism"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-attacks-opposition-leader-eisenkot-decries-jewish-terrorism</link><description>
Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were set on fire in three villages in the occupied West Bank. Israeli soldiers were deployed to the area following the attacks, which local residents said were carried out by Israeli settlers. Gadi Eisenkot, a rival of outgoing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, condemned the acts on X, describing them as “Jewish terrorism”. Antonia Kerrigan reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/800f91a6-e690-11f1-94e1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-160919-161053-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/800f91a6-e690-11f1-94e1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-160919-161053-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">850a0628-e690-11f1-9770-d1608150d187</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:25:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel investigates West Bank fires</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-investigates-west-bank-fires</link><description>
Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were vandalised and set on fire in four villages in the occupied West Bank, in attacks local activists say were carried out by Israeli settlers. Around eight vehicles were reportedly torched and racist slogans sprayed on walls, prompting Israeli soldiers and police to deploy to the area. The attacks come amid a surge in settler violence since the outbreak of the Gaza war in October 2023, with more than 1,100 Palestinians killed by Israeli soldiers or settlers in the West Bank since then, according to an AFP tally. They also follow recent sanctions announced by the UK and Australia against eight Israeli companies involved in settlement activity. France 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky shares further details from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f8b8c1ac-e679-11f1-8017-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-140613-140959-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f8b8c1ac-e679-11f1-8017-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-140613-140959-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdc5c032-e679-11f1-804f-f99043976363</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:47:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Bahrain accuses Iran of striking industrial site as tankers hit in Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-bahrain-accuses-iran-of-striking-industrial-site-as-tankers-hit-in-hormuz</link><description>
Bahrain accused Iran of striking a civilian industrial site on Saturday evening, as two tankers were hit in the Strait of Hormuz. Tehran reported shooting down a US drone amid stalled efforts to end the war. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30f63712-e624-11f1-976a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/c0934c40446967fd901759e5363f0c2bf9251a33.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30f63712-e624-11f1-976a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/c0934c40446967fd901759e5363f0c2bf9251a33.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31c5b4d8-e624-11f1-a020-0f3a5ebf3e34</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:24:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30f63712-e624-11f1-976a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/c0934c40446967fd901759e5363f0c2bf9251a33.jpg">© STR, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Eisenkot invites Netanyahu’s party for ‘marathon’ Israeli coalition talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261121-eisenkot-invites-netanyahu-s-party-for-marathon-israeli-coalition-talks</link><description>
Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has invited caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu's right-wing Likud party for coalition talks, his centrist Yashar party said Saturday. The "marathon series of talks" starts Sunday, the party said, adding that the move reflected a commitment to form "the broadest possible government" after the October election failed to deliver an outright winner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70936d94-e5e9-11f1-943b-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6U96RP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70936d94-e5e9-11f1-943b-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6U96RP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e61ef70-e5eb-11f1-a29b-5f44caa99dc9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:49:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70936d94-e5e9-11f1-943b-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6U96RP.jpg">© Ilia Yefimovich, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Endurance athlete swims in Hormuz Strait</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/endurance-athlete-swims-in-hormuz-strait</link><description>
The Strait of Hormuz remains largely blocked, with Iran attacking vessels attempting to cross it. As concerns grow over the environmental impact of the war, with toxic chemicals spreading through the air and sea, one swimmer and ocean advocate has gone a step further than issuing warnings: he plunged into the polluted and dangerous waters of the strait, calling on all sides to end the conflict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00399db4-e5c3-11f1-8eee-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-141231-141431-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00399db4-e5c3-11f1-8eee-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-141231-141431-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">056f3d7a-e5c3-11f1-b992-b90a38c59525</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:02:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthis launch strikes on Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-launch-strikes-on-saudi-arabia</link><description>
Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen continue to exchange strikes with the Saudi-led coalition. The coalition said it intercepted and destroyed three ballistic missiles fired towards Riyadh early on Saturday. It marks the second Houthi attack on the Saudi capital in recent days, following Saudi-led strikes on Houthi targets in Yemen. Yuka Royer has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/778980c6-e58e-11f1-b8cd-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091902-092039-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/778980c6-e58e-11f1-b8cd-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091902-092039-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c72fb9e-e58e-11f1-a931-1d57297cb463</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:49:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Houthis target Riyadh after Saudi coalition's 'special operation'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261120-yemen-s-houthis-target-riyadh-after-saudi-coalition-s-special-operation</link><description>
Yemen's Houthi rebels launched strikes on Riyadh on Saturday after Saudi-led coalition air raids on Yemen, escalating a months-long surge in cross-border attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/43dab966-e511-11f1-b7af-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/44975f13e4cedc724dc3005a9fa1d30c73841d8b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/43dab966-e511-11f1-b7af-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/44975f13e4cedc724dc3005a9fa1d30c73841d8b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">453b2db8-e511-11f1-954d-5137e52b96c5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:36:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/43dab966-e511-11f1-b7af-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/44975f13e4cedc724dc3005a9fa1d30c73841d8b.jpg">© Ansurallah media centre, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iraqi security forces deploy in Hezbollah stronghold under compromise deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261120-iraqi-security-forces-to-deploy-in-hezbollah-stronghold-under-compromise-deal</link><description>
Iraqi security forces deployed ​in the Kataib Hezbollah stronghold of Jurf al-Sakhar, state media said on Friday, under a compromise deal brokered by Shi'ite politicians. Iraq's prime minister ordered a security intervention earlier this week after accusing the Iran-backed militia of smuggling state-owned oil worth ⁠hundreds of millions of dollars.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d70c954-e4bb-11f1-9f2f-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321593824833.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d70c954-e4bb-11f1-9f2f-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321593824833.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8fd3f12-e4bc-11f1-9ec1-9748c2288644</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:37:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d70c954-e4bb-11f1-9f2f-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321593824833.jpg">© Anmar Khalil, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Skyscraper in Riyadh damaged as Saudi Arabia reports surge in new Houthi attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-skyscraper-in-riyadh-damaged-as-saudi-arabia-reports-surge-in-new-houthi-attacks</link><description>
A skyscraper in Saudi Arabia's capital Riyadh was damaged on Thursday after the Gulf country reported new attacks by Yemen's Houthis. Witnesses said the city's Public Investment Fund Tower, which showcases Saudi Arabia's economic ambitions, was "damaged across several floors, with windows blown out". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/889a1214-e3ee-11f1-801f-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6BN49E.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/889a1214-e3ee-11f1-801f-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6BN49E.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2a2cb846-e3ec-11f1-b561-cdbc4a9464ea</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:58:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/889a1214-e3ee-11f1-801f-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6BN49E.jpg">© Fayez Nureldine, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gaza: Israel launched new offensive on Nuseirat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-israel-launched-new-offensive-on-nuseirat</link><description>
Israeli tanks have moved east of the Nuseirat refugee camp in central Gaza, with witnesses reporting heavy shelling, gunfire and airstrikes as the Israeli military says it has launched an operation in a Hamas-controlled area. Strikes killed at least three people on Wednesday, and displaced families are fleeing again, saying there is no real ceasefire. Israel and Hamas accuse each other of breaking the truce in force since October 2025, while Gadi Eisenkot tries to form a government after inconclusive elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cb17a8e-e3ec-11f1-8605-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-061552-061743-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cb17a8e-e3ec-11f1-8605-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-061552-061743-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">820c9a0e-e3ec-11f1-98f3-2567f0c1ed5f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:50:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East crisis poses 'largest threat' to energy security in history, warns IEA</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-middle-east-crisis-energy-security-iea</link><description>
The International Energy Agency said on Thursday that the Middle East crisis triggered by US and Israeli strikes on Iran in February posed the “largest threat” to energy security in history. It warned that consumers were bearing more of the costs as Iran’s blockade of the Strait of Hormuz disrupted oil shipments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfcf9412-e37f-11f1-92da-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26318617092767.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfcf9412-e37f-11f1-92da-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26318617092767.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b9d06268-e3bf-11f1-a10b-a78e24423621</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:11:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfcf9412-e37f-11f1-92da-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26318617092767.jpg">© Amirhosein Khorgooi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli army launches ground operation in Hamas-controlled area of Gaza</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-in-hamas-controlled-area-of-gaza</link><description>
The Israeli military said it had launched an operation on Wednesday in a Hamas-controlled area of central Gaza, where an AFP journalist saw Israeli tanks position themselves east of the Nuseirat refugee camp. The rare ground operation comes after inconclusive Israeli elections, with the opposition's Gadi Eisenkot trying to form a government without caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who has built his brand on saying he will ensure Israel's security. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c27f5ac4-e368-11f1-97ec-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321586490001.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c27f5ac4-e368-11f1-97ec-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321586490001.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dd05d4d4-e388-11f1-b338-bba3e21069a0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:55:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Writer Etgar Keret: 'The Israel my parents dreamed of' is still possible, but not under Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261118-netanyahu-s-only-2-tickets-are-racism-or-starting-a-war-he-stopped-acting-as-a-democratic-player</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Israeli writer and filmmaker Etgar Keret, author of "The Seven Good Years". Keret argues that Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is seeking to remain in power, at any cost, including delegitimising Arab parties and prolonging conflict. "For him, it could be a never-ending war as long as he's in power. He has no incentive to stop it," our guest warns.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc28fae4-e43e-11f1-b9f8-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-09964174.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc28fae4-e43e-11f1-b9f8-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-09964174.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9436c6a0-e388-11f1-b2a0-bb68cd9c3227</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:45:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Gazans flee shelters as Israeli army launches ground operation beyond Yellow Line</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-gazans-flee-shelters-as-israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-beyond-yellow-line</link><description>
Palestinians fled their tents and shelters in central Gaza on Wednesday after Israel launched a rare ground operation in an area it withdrew ​from under a ‌2025 ceasefire. The Israeli army said it crossed the Yellow Line separating Israeli and Hamas-controlled areas "to remove a threat posed to IDF troops operating in the Gaza Strip". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/291a44ea-e375-11f1-8738-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T145851Z-876917872-RC2DQOALE3WH-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/291a44ea-e375-11f1-8738-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T145851Z-876917872-RC2DQOALE3WH-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">946c2080-e369-11f1-8169-7b555491c4b4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:03:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/291a44ea-e375-11f1-8738-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T145851Z-876917872-RC2DQOALE3WH-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg">© Mahmoud Issa, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen: Why the Houthis may besiege Aden rather than storm it</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-yemen-why-the-houthis-may-besiege-aden-rather-than-storm-it</link><description>
Bolstered by their recent military successes, Houthi rebels this week advanced close to the southern port city of Aden, the interim capital of the internationally recognised Yemeni government. Amid territorial ambitions, regional rivalries, and divisions within government forces, the potential fall of this stronghold could permanently alter the balance of power in the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a907106-e35a-11f1-a33f-dbb3dc175088</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:55:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg">© Abdulnasser Alseddik, AP</source><dc:creator>Marc DAOU</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Loud blast rocks Riyadh as Saudi-led coalition says it intercepted Houthi missiles</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-middle-east-live-kuwait-bahrain-report-drone-and-missile-attacks</link><description>
A powerful explosion rattled homes in Riyadh on Wednesday, journalists and residents said, as the Saudi-led coalition fighting Yemen's Houthis said they intercepted two cruise missiles fired by the Iran-backed militia. In Gaza, the Israeli military launched a rare ground operation in a Hamas-controlled area, leading dozens of families to flee their tents and shelters. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06b7fa46-86d2-11f1-8e4f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26198630293275.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06b7fa46-86d2-11f1-8e4f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26198630293275.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1668ed4-e2f4-11f1-bc21-b5a4f32090d0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:06:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06b7fa46-86d2-11f1-8e4f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26198630293275.jpg">© Osamah Abdulrahman, AP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
